{
 "factor_id": "F105_std_fangzheng_covamt",
 "sweep": "s2",
 "rule": "The test-period read for a batch sweep -- by a rule written before looking, with no judgement in it.\n\nFrom ``runs/<fid>/sweep_<tag>.json`` (train / valid only) it picks, mechanically:\n\n* ``v_base`` (the original) and ``k_known`` (the known-family benchmark), always;\n* the best variant of each of the 3 best KINDS (structure / leaf / memory / shape / neutral /\n  hypothesis ...), ranked by pure-long Sharpe on the user's training period, among variants that\n  pass the gates (cov >= 0.95, dist >= 0.5) and whose long leg is positive on BOTH train and valid;\n* the two best candidates BUILT ON the known family (overlays, screens, or any hypothesis that contains\n  it) -- reported apart, because they are the known family plus a tilt or minus a screen;\n* ``k_known_xfrozen``, the generic screen (known family, never the frozen-quote names), as their benchmark.\n\nOnly these are scored on the holdout (the user's test period), in the user's convention: sign and\nhalf-life fitted on the user's training period, pure long book net of 15 bp.  The read is ledgered.",
 "picks": [
  "seg_xfrozen_m",
  "iso_A",
  "h_ac_tiebreak"
 ],
 "overlay": [
  "h_atom_std_max3",
  "scr_xhi_p"
 ],
